    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed schedule today, forcing a defensive posture as our primary offensive engine rests. With elite producers like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** absent due to team off-days, and **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined on the IL, our floor is significantly compromised. Among the limited active options, **Andy Pages** (43.41) edges out **Drake Baldwin** (40.51) as the most viable start. While both are suppressed by a difficult matchup against Cease and his elite 2.96 xERA, **Andy Pages** benefits from slightly better underlying Statcast metrics and a higher projected xwOBA, keeping him just above the marginal threshold despite hitting 8th in the order.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved weighing the raw potential of our depth pieces against the high-skill ceiling of the opposing pitching. While **Drake Baldwin** remains in the lineup as our C1, his score of 40.51 reflects the heavy penalty of batting 9th against a pitcher of Cease\u2019s caliber. Had there been any surplus of elite sprint-speed prospects like **Nasim Nunez** or **Cole Carrigg** active today, they likely would have superseded **Drake Baldwin** purely on the necessity of chasing stolen bases, our scarcest category. Today is strictly an exercise in damage control; with no major lineup advantages for players like **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, or **Heliot Ramos**, we are essentially preserving game caps until the core of our roster returns to action tomorrow.",
